<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasir Pasha al-Sa'dun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasir Pasha al-Sa'dun was a sheikh of the Sa'dun family, rulers of the Muntafiq tribal confederation of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. Under the Ottoman reforms of the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midhat-pasha">Midhat Pasha</a> around 1870 he accepted office as the first governor of the new Muntafiq sanjak and founded the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasiriyah">Nasiriyah</a>, named after him, as its capital, turning the sheikhs into landlords and officials.</p></div>
